{% load public_url_tags %}
{% comment %}
Persistent trust-center nav, rendered under the brand header on every public
page.

A reader who lands on an advisory or a component page from a search result or a
customer email has no other way back to the workspace root — the logo is a link,
but nothing says so. This makes "where am I and how do I get back" answerable
from any page.

Renders nothing when no workspace can be resolved, which is how the public pages
that are not part of a trust center (standalone document and VDP pages) opt out
without needing to know about this file.
{% endcomment %}
{% workspace_public_url as tc_home_url %}
{% workspace_advisories_url as tc_advisories_url %}
{% if tc_home_url %}
    <nav class="tc-topnav" aria-label="Trust center">
        <div class="tc-topnav-inner">
            <a class="tc-topnav-item {% if request.path == tc_home_url %}is-current{% endif %}"
               href="{{ tc_home_url }}"
               {% if request.path == tc_home_url %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                <i class="fas fa-house" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Overview
            </a>
            {% if tc_advisories_url %}
                {# startswith, so an advisory detail page still marks the section current. #}
                <a class="tc-topnav-item {% if tc_advisories_url in request.path %}is-current{% endif %}"
                   href="{{ tc_advisories_url }}"
                   {% if tc_advisories_url in request.path %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                    <i class="fas fa-shield-halved" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    Security advisories
                </a>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </nav>
{% endif %}
